    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. Changes made:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean column (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`) defaulting to `false`, with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`.\n\n2. **OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically. It appears in `GET` responses.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n   - `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and saves the owner (retaining the row) instead of removing it, still returning `204` (2xx).\n   - `findExistingOwner` \u2014 the shared helper behind both the identity-key duplicate check (`rejectDuplicateIdentity`) and the household duplicate check (`rejectHouseholdDuplicate`) \u2014 now filters out owners flagged deleted, so a would-be duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `deleted` column. Used `DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` ordering for h2/hsqldb (HSQLDB, the profile the tests actually run under, requires `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL`) and `NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE` for mysql/postgres.\n\nBehavior verified by the two acceptance tests: a created owner reads back `deleted: false`; after `DELETE` the owner is still returned by `GET` with `deleted: true`; and re-creating an owner whose only match is soft-deleted succeeds.\n\nNote: I mirrored the schema change across all four DB dialects for consistency, though only the hsqldb schema is exercised by the test profile. The inactive JDBC repository implementation was left untouched since the active profile is `spring-data-jpa`.",
